      "versionNonce": 900896,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1794800000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "• Why 1: Why do I go so far to have everything at hand before I\nstart? (Claude)",
      "originalText": "• Why 1: Why do I go so far to have everything at hand before I start? (Claude)",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "a18-card-gw-t12",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1432.0,
      "y": 6753.0,
      "width": 744.0,
      "height": 125.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#f1ece2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "grp-a18-card-gw"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bQW",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 900897,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 900898,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1794800000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "• Because 1 (Anna): not having everything planned out means I will\nfail; I need to understand what's beneath; because I cant imagine\nhow to get to the goal and it feels like the missing links are\nhidden in what I dont know whenever I try to figure out how to\nwrite out the puzzle so I can solve it. I cant grasp the puzzle.",
      "originalText": "• Because 1 (Anna): not having everything planned out means I will fail; I need to understand what's beneath; because I cant imagine how to get to the goal and it feels like the missing links are hidden in what I dont know whenever I try to figure out how to write out the puzzle so I can solve it. I cant grasp the puzzle.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "a18-card-gw-t13",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1432.0,
      "y": 6886.0,
      "width": 744.0,
      "height": 25.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#f1ece2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "grp-a18-card-gw"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bQX",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 900899,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 900900,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1794800000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "• Why 2: Why can't I grasp the puzzle? (Claude)",
      "originalText": "• Why 2: Why can't I grasp the puzzle? (Claude)",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "a18-card-gw-t14",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1432.0,
      "y": 6919.0,
      "width": 744.0,
      "height": 250.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#f1ece2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "grp-a18-card-gw"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bQY",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 900901,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 900902,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1794800000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "• Because 2 (Anna): learning places are top-down; I haven't found\nan approach that fits me; in many places to see the puzzle I first\nhave to know what the puzzle entails as in all its bits and\npieces. a word means little to me. what is an os? its and\noperating system that makes your device run. Can I build it myself\nwith those words? No, because what is an operating system in\ndetail? What is a device? what does it mean for a deivce to run?\nThe puzzle is so overly simplified and finding the right sources\nthat explain the parts of the words, sentences, abstracts etc\nbeyond just word is really hard.",
      "originalText": "• Because 2 (Anna): learning places are top-down; I haven't found an approach that fits me; in many places to see the puzzle I first have to know what the puzzle entails as in all its bits and pieces. a word means little to me. what is an os? its and operating system that makes your device run. Can I build it myself with those words? No, because what is an operating system in detail? What is a device? what does it mean for a deivce to run? The puzzle is so overly simplified and finding the right sources that explain the parts of the words, sentences, abstracts etc beyond just word is really hard.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "a18-card-gw-t15",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1432.0,
      "y": 7177.0,
      "width": 744.0,
      "height": 50.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#f1ece2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "grp-a18-card-gw"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bQZ",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 900903,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 900904,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1794800000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "• Why 3: Why is it so hard to find sources that explain the parts\nbeneath the words? (Claude)",
      "originalText": "• Why 3: Why is it so hard to find sources that explain the parts beneath the words? (Claude)",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "a18-card-gw-t16",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1432.0,
      "y": 7235.0,
      "width": 744.0,
      "height": 350.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#f1ece2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "grp-a18-card-gw"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bQa",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 900905,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 900906,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1794800000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "• Because 3 (Anna): my fear of missing important facts;\nself-taught, sources of different quality; they assume knowledge I\nlack; its all either just text, just theory, just video, a lot of\nstuff that is made for the 99% of people that apparently\nunderstand and learn that way. It doesnt stick, it leaves more\nquestions that what I started with. I want to know what a and b is\nin a+b=x where x is operating system, and then solve for a and b,\nbut those are apparently lost to time and space and\ninaccessibility when trying to learn for myself. along the way i\nfind out there isnt really an x, or its called things under many\ndifferent names, or a+b=x doesnt even exist in that form, and\nthere is so many barricades to accessible learning everywhere that\nis so foundationnal and just built in a not fun and engaging way\nfor the masses that it drains me to keep digging.",
      "originalText": "• Because 3 (Anna): my fear of missing important facts; self-taught, sources of different quality; they assume knowledge I lack; its all either just text, just theory, just video, a lot of stuff that is made for the 99% of people that apparently understand and learn that way. It doesnt stick, it leaves more questions that what I started with. I want to know what a and b is in a+b=x where x is operating system, and then solve for a and b, but those are apparently lost to time and space and inaccessibility when trying to learn for myself. along the way i find out there isnt really an x, or its called things under many different names, or a+b=x doesnt even exist in that form, and there is so many barricades to accessible learning everywhere that is so foundationnal and just built in a not fun and engaging way for the masses that it drains me to keep digging.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
